  "id": "electronics.industrial-control.industrial-control-architecture",
  "name": "Industrial Control Architecture",
  "level": "process",
  "parent": "electronics.industrial-control",
  "description": "Integrated industrial-control architecture — the ISA-95/Purdue hierarchy (field, sensing, control, supervisory, enterprise), the sensor-to-actuator control chain, partitioning of a plant into controller zones, determinism vs event-driven design, hardwired safety layers outside the PLC, and the fieldbus-to-Ethernet-to-WAN communication hierarchy that ties relay logic, PLCs, VFDs, SCADA, and HMI into one coherent system.",
  "timeline": "Years 35-55",
